ComplytEX (SaaS Agent)
User Manual – Step-by-Step Guide with Screenshot Placeholders
Version 1.1

NOTE ABOUT IMAGES
- This document includes clearly marked "Screenshot:" placeholders.
- Open this file in Microsoft Word and replace each placeholder line by
  inserting an actual screenshot from your running application.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. LOGIN & AUTHENTICATION
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

1.1 Login Page (`/login.html`)

Screenshot: [Insert full-page screenshot of Login screen here]

PURPOSE
- Sign in with your email and password, or use one of the demo accounts.

HOW TO OPEN
1. In your browser, go to your app URL (e.g. `http://localhost:3000`).
2. Click the "Login" link in the top area of the Home page, or open
   `/login.html` directly.

FIELDS
- Email – your login email.
- Password – your login password.

STEPS – SIGN IN WITH NORMAL ACCOUNT
1. Type your **Email** into the Email box.
2. Type your **Password** into the Password box.
3. Click the **Sign In** button.
4. Watch the status box below the button:
   - If it turns green and shows "Signed in!", you will be redirected to the
     Owner Dashboard or another page configured by the backend.
   - If it turns red with an error message, correct the problem (e.g. wrong
     password) and try again.

STEPS – SIGN IN AS DEMO USER
1. Scroll to the **Demo Accounts** section.
2. Find the role you want (e.g. **Owner**, **HR Manager**, **Buyer**, etc.).
3. Click the **Login as ...** button for that role.
4. The Email and Password fields will be filled for you.
5. The system will automatically attempt login; if not, click **Sign In**.

TIP
- After logging in as different demo users, you can see how the same modules
  behave under different roles.


-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2. HOME / DEMO DASHBOARD
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

2.1 SaaS Agent Dashboard (`/index.html`)

Screenshot: [Insert screenshot of Home / SaaS Agent Dashboard here]

PURPOSE
- Test that your Azure SQL database is reachable.
- Demonstrate basic CRUD on a demo Contacts table.

HOW TO OPEN
1. Go to `/` or `/index.html` in your browser.

SECTIONS
- Top links: Login, Register, Owner Dashboard, Employees, Roles, Support,
  Billing.
- Database Connection card.
- Contact Management card.
- Contacts List card.

STEPS – TEST DATABASE CONNECTION
1. Locate the **Database Connection** card.
2. Click the **Test Database Connection** button.
3. Wait a few seconds.
4. Confirm that a green success box appears with details:
   - Database name
   - Server name
   - Number of tables
   - Connection time
5. If a red error box appears, verify your backend configuration and try again.

STEPS – ADD A CONTACT
1. Find the **Contact Management** card.
2. In the **Contact name** field, type a name (e.g. `John Demo`).
3. Click **Add Contact**.
4. Watch the status area just below the form:
   - A green success message should appear with the new total count of
     contacts.
5. To see the full list, click **Refresh List** in the same card.

STEPS – EDIT A CONTACT
1. Scroll to the **Contacts List** card.
2. Click **Refresh List** if you don’t see any rows yet.
3. Find the row of the contact you want to edit.
4. Click the **Edit** button for that row.
5. In the **Edit Contact** popup/modal:
   - Change the name in the input field.
   - Click **Save Changes**.
6. After a short delay, the popup will close and the list will refresh.

STEPS – DELETE A CONTACT
1. In the Contacts List, find the contact you want to remove.
2. Click the **Delete** button on that row.
3. Confirm the browser confirmation dialog.
4. The contact will be removed from the list.

STEPS – CLEAR ALL CONTACTS
1. Go to the **Contact Management** card.
2. Click the **Clear All** button.
3. Confirm the warning dialog. This action cannot be undone.
4. The list in **Contacts List** card will become empty.


-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
3. OWNER DASHBOARD
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

3.1 Owner Dashboard (`/dashboard.html`)

Screenshot: [Insert screenshot of Owner Dashboard page here]

PURPOSE
- Show high-level metrics (Employees, Customers, Suppliers, Certifications)
  and module list for a specific tenant.

HOW TO OPEN
1. Log in.
2. Navigate to `/dashboard.html` or click **Owner Dashboard** from Home.

FIELDS
- Tenant ID – numeric tenant identifier.
- Business Type – select from Manufacturer, Buyer, Supplier, etc.

STEPS – LOAD A TENANT SUMMARY
1. In the **Tenant ID** box, enter your tenant’s ID (for demo data, use the ID
   provided with your sample DB).
2. Optionally choose a **Business Type** from the dropdown.
3. Click the **Load** button.
4. Wait for the page to show:
   - Tenant name and business type under the input row.
   - Metrics on the cards (Employees, Customers, Suppliers, Certifications).
   - A list of Modules in the grid below.

HOW TO READ THE MODULES GRID
- Each tile represents a major module (HR, CRM, Accounting, Safety, etc.).
- Modules may be visually highlighted when the selected Business Type makes
  them more important.

NEXT STEPS
- From the top links or main app shell, continue into detailed modules:
  - Employees → manage users.
  - Roles → configure permissions.
  - Business Setup → configure company details.


-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
4. APPLICATION SHELL
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

4.1 App Shell (`/app.html`)

Screenshot: [Insert screenshot of App Shell with left module menu here]

PURPOSE
- Provide a single, modern shell with left-side navigation and main content
  loaded into an iframe, so users can jump across modules easily.

HOW TO OPEN
1. After logging in, go to `/app.html`.

STEPS – OPEN A MODULE FROM THE SHELL
1. On the left, locate the **Modules** card.
2. Click a module, for example **HR & Payroll**.
3. Watch the main panel on the right:
   - It will load the corresponding page (e.g. `/hr/index.html`).
4. To switch modules, click another item (e.g. **Accounting**, **CRM**).

TIP
- The URL hash changes (for example `#/hr` or `#/crm`), so you can bookmark or
  share direct links to a specific module within the shell.


-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
5. BUSINESS SETUP (PROFILE)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

5.1 Company Profile – Head Office (in `/profile.html`)

Screenshot: [Insert screenshot of Business Setup / Head Office section here]

PURPOSE
- Store the main company details (address, capacity, wages, product lines,
  logo) used by invoices and other modules.

HOW TO OPEN
1. In the App Shell, choose **Business Setup**.
2. Ensure the Head Office/Company Profile tab is active.

STEPS – FILL BASIC COMPANY INFORMATION
1. Under "Head Office Address", fill:
   - Address 1 (required)
   - Address 2 (optional)
   - City
   - State/Province
   - Postal Code
2. Under "Total No. of Employees", enter the total count of staff.
3. Enter capacity information:
   - Capacity Type (e.g. "Pieces/day").
   - Capacity Qty.
   - Minimum Order Qty.
4. Under "Sales Profit", enter:
   - Sales Profit Type (e.g., "%" or "Fixed")
   - Sales Profit Value (a number).
5. Fill wage/age fields:
   - Minimum Wage
   - Minimum Age
   - Retirement Age.
6. Under "Product You Deal In", tick **Garments** and/or **Home Textile**.

STEPS – UPLOAD COMPANY LOGO
1. In the "Upload a Logo" area, click the file input.
2. Select a PNG/JPEG logo file from your computer.
3. Wait a moment;
   - The file is uploaded to the backend.
   - The preview area shows the stored logo.

STEPS – MANAGE PRODUCT LINES
1. In the "Product Line" section, type a line name in the input
   (e.g. "T-Shirts").
2. Click **Add**.
3. The line will appear in the list below with a **Delete** button.
4. To remove a line, click **Delete** on that row and confirm.

STEPS – SAVE COMPANY PROFILE
1. After entering all fields, click the **Save Company Profile** button.
2. Wait for alert/confirmation message.
3. Re-open the page to confirm values are loaded correctly.


5.2 Warehouses (in `/profile.html`)

Screenshot: [Insert screenshot of Warehouses list and New Warehouse modal]

PURPOSE
- Record one or more warehouse, store, shipping, or billing addresses.

HOW TO OPEN
1. In Business Setup, click the Warehouse tab or choose it via left buttons.

STEPS – VIEW EXISTING WAREHOUSES
1. Scroll to the **Warehouses** section.
2. The list shows each warehouse with:
   - Name
   - Type (Retail/Wholesale/etc.)
   - Full address
   - Delete button.

STEPS – ADD A NEW WAREHOUSE
1. Click **New Warehouse**.
2. In the popup form, enter:
   - Warehouse Name.
   - Address Type (Shipping, Warehouse, Store, Billing).
   - Warehouse Type (Retail, Wholesale, Distribution, Store, Fulfillment).
   - Address 1, Address 2.
   - City, State, Postal Code.
   - Country (select from dropdown).
3. Click **Save**.
4. Confirm that the modal closes and the new warehouse appears in the list.

STEPS – DELETE A WAREHOUSE
1. In the list, find the warehouse to remove.
2. Click the **Delete** button.
3. Confirm the deletion.


5.3 Spaces (in `/profile.html`)

Screenshot: [Insert screenshot of Spaces table and New Space modal]

PURPOSE
- Maintain dimensional and safety metadata for each separate physical space
  (room, floor area, etc.).

STEPS – FILTER AND EXPORT SPACES
1. To search: type keywords in the **Search** box (e.g., "Cutting Floor").
2. To export CSV: click **Export Excel**.
3. To print/export as PDF: click **Export PDF** (opens a new window to print).

STEPS – CREATE A NEW SPACE
1. Click **New Space**.
2. In the modal dialog, complete at least:
   - Space name (e.g., "Cutting Floor 1").
   - Type (e.g., "Production", "Warehouse").
3. Optionally set:
   - Purpose, width, length, height, unit, floor, capacity, ventilation,
     number of doors and windows.
4. (Optional) Choose an **Emergency Exit plan** image.
5. Click **Save**.
6. If an exit-plan image was selected, it will be uploaded in a second step.
7. Close the modal; confirm the new space is visible in the table.

STEPS – DELETE A SPACE
1. In the spaces table, locate the row.
2. Click **Delete**.
3. Confirm the action.


5.4 Assets, Certifications, Unions

For each of these tabs in Business Setup, the workflow is similar:
- Use **Search** to filter existing rows.
- Use **New / Add New** button to open a modal.
- Fill labeled fields.
- Click **Save** to create a record.
- Use **Delete** buttons in the table to remove records.
- Export tables via **Export Excel/PDF** where available.

Screenshots: [Insert one screenshot for Assets, one for Certifications,
  and one for Unions lists and modals]


5.5 Business Agent (embedded in `/profile.html`)

Screenshot: [Insert screenshot of Business Agent panel]

STEPS – USE BUSINESS AGENT
1. Scroll to the **BUSINESS AGENT** panel in Business Setup.
2. Optionally type instructions or context in the large text area.
3. (Optional) Pick a file (e.g. existing safety or audit report) in the
   upload control.
4. Click **Submit**.
5. Wait for a "Working..." indicator to disappear.
6. Review the result panel:
   - Extracted Facts
   - Proposed Changes (which tables, what actions, what data).
7. To apply changes:
   - Click **Approve & Apply** (this may write data into your database).
8. To discard:
   - Click **Reject** and confirm.


-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
6. EMPLOYEES & ROLES
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

6.1 Employees (`/employees.html`)

Screenshot: [Insert screenshot of Employees page showing form and table]

STEPS – LOAD EMPLOYEES FOR A TENANT
1. Enter your **Tenant ID** at the top.
2. Click **Load**.
3. Confirm the table below shows employees or "Empty".

STEPS – ADD A NEW EMPLOYEE
1. In the **Add employee** section, fill:
   - Email
   - Full name
   - Password (optional)
   - Title (e.g., "HR Manager")
   - Role name (optional – can be created later in Roles module).
2. Click **Add**.
3. If successful, the new employee appears in the table.

STEPS – VIEW EMPLOYEE ROLES
1. In the table, look at the **Roles** column to see assigned roles.
2. Use the **Roles** page to modify role definitions.


6.2 Roles (`/roles.html`)

Screenshot: [Insert screenshot of Roles page: permissions list and roles table]

STEPS – LOAD ROLES
1. Enter your **Tenant ID**.
2. Click **Load**.
3. View existing roles in the **Existing roles** table.

STEPS – CREATE A ROLE
1. Under **Create role**, type a **Role name** (e.g., "Safety Officer").
2. In the permission list:
   - Tick each permission code that this role should have.
3. Click **Create role**.
4. Confirm it appears in the **Existing roles** table.

STEPS – ASSIGN A ROLE TO A USER
1. Get the **User ID** from the Employees page.
2. Get the **Role ID** from the roles list (usually shown by the backend; if
   not, use the order or check the DB).
3. In the **Assign role to user** section, fill **User ID** and **Role ID**.
4. Click **Assign**.
5. Return to Employees to verify their roles.


